  "notes": "USAGE:\nかき{混|ま}ぜる is a compound verb formed from かく (to stir/scratch) + {混|ま}ぜる (to mix). It implies more vigorous mixing than {混|ま}ぜる alone. Commonly used in cooking instructions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- よくかき{混|ま}ぜる (stir well)\n- ぐるぐるかき{混|ま}ぜる (stir round and round)\n- スプーンでかき{混|ま}ぜる (stir with a spoon)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{混|ま}ぜる focuses on combining ingredients, while かき{混|ま}ぜる emphasizes the stirring action itself. {攪拌|かくはん}する is a more technical or scientific term for stirring.",
